{
  "name": "My Garage Is Always Cold: How Can I Insulate It Better?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "If your garage feels like a freezer in winter and an oven in summer, better insulation is definitely the answer! The key to improving its comfort lies in a few critical steps. First, you'll want to inspect your existing framing and sheathing to make sure everything's solid and ready for insulation. Next, choosing the right type and thickness of insulation for your wall cavities is super important; it needs to fill the space without being compressed, which reduces its effectiveness. Carefully installing it so there are no major gaps around wiring, pipes, or framing irregularities will prevent those pesky cold spots. Finally, once the insulation is in, you'll need to think about the interior wall covering, especially if your garage is attached to your home, as fire-rated drywall might be required. Getting these steps right can drastically improve your garage's temperature control and even lower your energy bills if it shares a wall with your living space. If you're looking to transform your chilly garage into a more usable space, HH Remodeling LLC can help you figure out the best insulation strategy for your home in the Denver area.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
